{
	title: 'Accept sequential commands in one tool call',
	spec: 'The native tool silently accepts multiple complete tool commands separated by top-level newlines, for any registered tools, in both provider calls and hal/tool direct mode. Guidance still teaches one command per call. Commands in one call execute sequentially in written order, not concurrently. Quoted strings, structured arguments and comments containing newlines or tool names are never split. Resolve all commands before dispatch so malformed or ambiguous input runs nothing. Each expanded command is durably recorded with its own result and normal approval, cancellation, background-job identity, unsafe-to-stop controls, file leases, complete errors and output. Expanded commands replay as ordinary native tool calls with their matching results. Runtime failures remain visible and later commands retain normal execution unless canceled or declined. Separate native calls retain existing concurrency and WAIT ordering. Invariant: clear requests must not fail solely because multiple complete commands share one native call. Regression cases include repeated BASH commands, multiple EDIT commands and mixed tools, sequential ordering, malformed trailing calls, multiline argument boundaries and approval.',
